  "A “loading” layer over a container or the whole page: a shade, a pane with the kit’s spinner and a message, a Cancel button when the work can be stopped. Nothing under it can be used meanwhile, and focus comes back afterwards.": "",
  "Over a container": "",
  "`target` names the component or element it covers; `value` (or `x-model`) shows and hides it, `show()` and `hide()` programmatically. `delay` keeps quick work from flashing it.": "",
  "Over the page, with Cancel": "",
  "Shade, pane and indicator": "",
  "It goes inside the container, over everything in it; the container is `aria-busy` and what is under the panel is inert: nothing there can be pressed or focused.": "",
  "Without a `target`, it covers the viewport and the rest of the page is inert.": "",
  "Focus that was under it waits on the panel (on the Cancel button when there is one) and goes back where it was when the panel hides.": "",
  "Quick work shows nothing: it comes after `delay`, and a hide before that cancels it.": "",
  "The kit’s spinner covers a container programmatically in one call (`Spinner.cover`); the load panel is the component with the pane, the message, the delay and the button.": "",
  "A `status` region: the message is read when the panel appears, and again when it changes.": "",
  "Decorative; the message says what is going on.": "",
  "`inert` and `aria-busy`, so readers skip it and nothing there takes a press or focus.": "",
  "The kit’s button, named in the kit language; Escape presses it.": "",
  "The layer. `data-shade`, `data-pane`, `data-page`.": "",
  "The pane.": "",
  "The spinner, the message and the button.": "",
  "Units: the layer (`shaded`), the pane (`shown`), the message.": "",
  "Place: the Cancel button’s look (`variant`).": "",
  "The least space to the edge of what it covers; the space between the indicator, the message and the button.": "",
  "What it covers: a component or an element; `null` covers the whole page.": "",
  "The message under the indicator. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "Shown or not; `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "Milliseconds before it shows; a hide before that shows nothing.": "",
  "Dims what it covers.": "",
  "The box behind the indicator and the message.": "",
  "The turning indicator (the kit’s spinner).": "",
  "A Cancel button in the pane; Escape presses it too.": "",
  "the kit’s “Cancel”": "",
  "The button’s text.": "",
  "A press on the shade hides it.": "",
  "It came on the screen (after its delay); it went.": "",
  "The Cancel button was pressed, or Escape; the panel hides after.": "",
